## Summary of Changes to `/Users/tma/repos/policy-system/spikes/pipeline-rag3/ingest.py`

### 1. Added `_normalise_regex()` function (lines 120-145)
- New function to handle regex shorthand `/.../i|s|m` syntax
- Returns `(pattern_str, additional_flags)` tuple
- Logs warning when shorthand is detected and stripped
- Strips leading `/` and trailing flag characters (`i`, `m`, `s`)
- Converts flags to `re.I`, `re.M`, `re.S` constants

### 2. Updated `--filter-regex` help text (lines 165-167)
**Before:**
```python
help="Case-insensitive regex selecting substantive chunks (default 'shall|should').")
```

**After:**
```python
help="Case-insensitive regex pattern (NOT shorthand — no delimiters/flags;\n"
     "e.g. shall|should, not /shall/i; default: shall|should)")
```

### 3. Updated `run()` function to use `_normalise_regex()` (lines 220-222)
**Before:**
```python
pred = re.compile(args.filter_regex, re.I)
```

**After:**
```python
pattern_str, additional_flags = _normalise_regex(args.filter_regex)
pred = re.compile(pattern_str, additional_flags | re.I)
chunk_select_note = f"substantive=/{pattern_str}/i, cap {args.substantive}"
```

